🔥 Ditch hybrid GGUF CPU offloading; use EXL2 3.25bpw precision quantization;
🔥 FlashInfer accelerates Multi-Head Latent Attention (MLA) kernels;
🔥 Time-to-first-token is 0.3s, sustained output reaches 52 tok/sec silently!

Docker commands and HuggingFace weights below👇

Most developers use Cursor only for single-file completion. Its true power shines when refactoring massive 10k+ LoC codebases:

📌 Rule 1: Configure `.cursorrules` to enforce immutable function signatures;
📌 Rule 2: Use `@codebase` to map circular dependencies and extract unified interfaces;
📌 Rule 3: Batch-refactor TypeScript types across 18 files with zero type errors!

Architecture diff and config snippets below👇

Two weeks of heavy production use with Windsurf Cascade:

Often compared with Cursor, but Cascade's 'Flow Tracking' takes a radically different architecture:

📌 Modify a core data model, and it silently synchronizes interface signatures across all referencing files without prompting;
📌 Built-in rollback snapshots: if test suites fail, it rewinds state and tries an alternate implementation pattern;
📌 Consumes 35% less memory than typical extension wrappers.

